     0009             (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00110         stkdepth            set       9
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00111         
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00112         * All functions (from the call table) are entered with the following parameters:
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00113         *   Y = pointer to function subroutine
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00114         *   X = pointer to "stkdepth" byte scratch variable area (same as stack pointer, which has allocated that extra memory)
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00115         *   U = pointer to 2nd parameter (first parameter after name itself)
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00116         *   D = # of parameters (NOTE: function name itself is always parameter 1)
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00117         
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00118         * Stack on entry to every function routine (with stkdepth set to 9):
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00119         *   $00-$08 / 00-08,s - temporary scratch var area
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00120         *   $09-$0A / 09-10,s - RTS address to BASIC09/RUNB
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00121         *   $0B-$0C / 11-12,s - # of parameters (including function name itself)
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00122         *   $0D-$0E / 13-14,s - pointer to 1st parameter's data (function name)
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00123         *   $0F-$10 / 15-16,s - length of first parameter
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00124         * From here on is optional, depending on the function being called, there can be up to 9 parameter pairs
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00125         * (pointer/value and length).
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00126         * The temporary stack uses 0,s as the path #, and 1,s + as the output buffer.
                      (s/basic09/gfx.asm):00127         
